{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This is an example of a package file. It installs itself as a ReaScript that does nothing but show "Hello World!" in REAPER's scripting console.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Packages may also include additional files specified using the @provides tag.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This text is the documentation shown when using ReaPack's "About this package" feature. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://commonmark.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Markdown
}}}
 {\i formatting} is supported.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Reaper Studio 7\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A collection of scripts that utilizes more hotkeys than mouseclicks for various editing actions that are lacking or aren't available natively to Reaper. If you dislike mouse-workflows or just want to do certain actions on a keyboard shortcut, then you'll like what we have here.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Alot of these script's editing features are inspired from various digital audio workstations that me and my team can't live without, but it's mainly "FL Studio" & "Ableton".\par}
}
